# Defect 2225, panel 230's R3, 2026-10-26: a `str` side is written at most 1,024
# bytes long, then ` ... N more bytes`, where the lldb formatter cuts a `str`
# (`editors/lldb/heroes_lldb.py`, `TEXT_BYTES`), so a side of a megabyte writes a
# line and not a megabyte. 600 copies of `ab` are 1,200 bytes: 176 left out.

function main()
    s = repeat("ab", to_u64(600).must())
    assert s == "ab"
